    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Both tests pass. Summary of the change:\n\n**Spec implemented:** `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\n**Changes (three small, cohesive edits):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it. (Kept it a plain string, matching the existing derived fields, to avoid coupling the mapper to a generated nested enum type.)\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`, exactly like the sibling derived fields (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, \u2026):\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java((owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()) ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n\n3. **`EmailDuplicates.java`** \u2014 added a guard so a *missing* email isn't treated as a duplicate. This was a necessary fix: seed owners carry `NULL` emails, and the old rule collapsed `null \u2192 \"\"`, so any no-email create returned 409 \u2014 breaking the `corePhoneWhenNoEmail` test (and the base's \"`ownerNode()` is accepted by every rule\" invariant). The guard matches the spec's \"email is optional; when present\u2026\".\n\nI kept structural impact low by adding behaviour as one-line expressions/guards on tiny units rather than growing any method or large class \u2014 no logic was added to the big `OwnerRestControllerV1`, and each touched function stays simple.",
